# Orbitype CMS

**Most important rule in this template.** Violations break rendering, security, or agent workflows.

## Sections contract

Every section object in CMS JSON:

```json
{
  "title": { "en": "..." },
  "_orbi": { "component": "SectionHero" }
}
```

- `_orbi` is **always last** in documentation examples; parsers do not require order
- `_orbi.component` must match a `Section*.astro` filename stem
- All other keys become props spread into the section (minus `_orbi` stripped by `AnySection`)
- Pass **`normalizeSections()`** on every `sections`, `sections_before`, `sections_after` read — Orbitype may store nested arrays `[[{...}]]`

## SQL access

- Single client: `orbitypeSql(sql, bindings)` in `src/lib/orbitype/client.ts`
- **Named bindings only** — never interpolate user input into SQL strings
- Every mutation includes **`RETURNING`** — responses contain only returned rows; no rowcount
- Install **`uid()` before tables** — see ADR-0011

## Error shapes (do not assume 401)

| Condition | Status | Body |
|-----------|--------|------|
| Missing API key | 400 | `text/plain` |
| Invalid API key | 404 | JSON `E_ROW_NOT_FOUND` |
| Bad route/method | 404 | JSON |

Always read error bodies with `.text()`. Never call `.json()` on errors blindly.

## MCP session discipline

Before any Orbitype MCP tool use in Cursor:

1. Export `ORBITYPE_SQL_API_KEY` (`pnpm run mcp:env`)
2. Reload MCP in Cursor
3. Call **`orbitype_get_context`** first to confirm connector scope
4. Use read-only `SELECT` for exploration; confirm with user before `INSERT`/`UPDATE`/`DELETE`/`DDL`

Safe workflow: context → read → propose SQL → user confirms → mutate with `RETURNING`.

## Mock and seed

- `ORBITYPE_MOCK=true` or missing key → seed data via `src/lib/orbitype/seed.ts`
- `findSeedPage(slug)` returns `null` for unknown slugs (404 in mock mode)
- `POST /api/setup/seed` populates live connector from same builders

## Templates

Composition: `[...before, ...page, ...after]`. See ADR-0013.
